%description:

Tcp.advertisedWindow:too-large -- a window above the largest scaled window stops the run with an error.

The claim: the code accepts at most 65535 << 14 = 1073725440 bytes with window scaling (RFC
7323 section 2.3: the shift count is at most 14).

The classes: unscaled (65535 and less: the default, and 14 * 536 = 7504 of LegacyTcp), scaled
(above 65535, with window scaling), unscalable (above 65535 without window scaling: an error),
too-large (above 65535 << 14 = 1073725440: an error). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value and sets the first offer;
TcpConnection::synWindow() limits the window of a SYN to 65535; the window scale of the
connection carries a larger window.

Host under test: host2. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.advertisedWindow
%# class: too-large
%# value: 1073741824
%# key: *.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpAdvertisedWindowTooLarge compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.advertisedWindow = 1073741824    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
advertisedWindow=1073741824 exceeds representable maximum 1073725440 with windowScalingFactor=-1
